# Local SDK configuration and build-system state.
local.properties
.gradle/
.kotlin/

# Generated build and packaged artifacts.
build/
**/build/
*.apk
*.aab
captures/
# dist/ holds release artifacts and must never be committed.
dist/
.cxx/

# Signing material. keystore.properties configures the upload key; neither the
# configuration nor any key file may ever be committed.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# Promo codes issued for this slot's promotions. A code is a free unlock of whatever the
# slot sells, so a downloaded batch is a pile of giveaways: it belongs beside the slot on
# one machine, never in a repository that can be cloned, forked, shared, or made public
# later. `store/console-answers.md` carries the reviewer instruction with a placeholder
# rather than a live code, so the committed pack has nothing to leak.
#
# Both names are listed because the console's own export is `promotion_codes.csv` while the
# factory's convention for the same file is `promo-codes.csv`, and a rule that covers only
# the second one leaves the console's real filename untracked-but-committable - which is how
# a batch of 100 codes sat staged for a commit on 2026-09-29.
promo-codes.csv
promotion_codes.csv

# Local environment and service credentials.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
google-services.json
play-service-account.json

# IDE-local files.
.idea/
*.iml

# Worker logs. `scripts/codex-run.mjs` writes a run's stdout beside its durable
# ledger under `.kiln/`, and a run started with the slot as its working directory
# leaves that output in the slot root instead. Those are machine-local build logs:
# they were committed once by hand and had to be removed, so they are ignored here
# and in the scaffold every new slot is copied from.
.kiln-*.log
